---
source: crates/baml_cli/src/describe_command_tests.rs
expression: output
---
as — Projects a value or type through an interface, and maps interface fields to class fields.

Syntax:
  // Field mapping inside an implements block.
  interface HasId {
    type Id
    id: Id
  }
  
  class User {
    implements HasId {
      type Id = string
      id as user_id
    }
    full_name: string
    user_id: string
  }
  
  function label(user: User) -> string {
    return user.as<HasId>.id
  }
  
  // Associated type projection in a type position.
  type UserId = (User as HasId).Id

Use `value.as<Interface>` when a class implements multiple interfaces with the same member name or when you need the interface view. Use `(Type as Interface).Assoc` for qualified associated type projection in a type position; do not write `Type.as<Interface>` as a type. Inside an `implements` block, `interface_field as class_field` maps an interface field to a differently named class field.
